  "description": "Mediterranean island (various polities 500–1768) that passed between Byzantine, Lombard, Frankish, Arab, Pisan, Genoese, and eventually French sovereignty; its mountainous interior supported pastoral clan societies that resisted external authority while coastal cities maintained commercial links with the mainland Italian city-states; Genoese rule (1284–1768) shaped modern Corsican culture before cession to France in the year of Napoleon's birth.",
